//Friend Class
A friend class is a class that is given permission to access the private and protected members of another class.

We use the friend keyword.

class A {
private:
    int x = 10;

    friend class B;
};

class B {
public:
    void show(A obj) {
        cout << obj.x;
    }
};

Here:

A → gives friendship to B
B → can access A's private x
B itself is not a child class of A

So:

A a;
B b;

b.show(a);  // 10
Important

Friendship is not inheritance.

A
↓ friend
B

does not mean B inherits from A.

Also, friendship is not automatically mutual: if B is a friend of A, that doesn't automatically make A a friend of B.

Simple definition:

Friend class = a class that is given permission to access another class's private and protected members.